# English in keco-simulation

- **User-visible text**: UI labels, buttons, placeholders, table headers, breadcrumbs, `message.*` / notifications, modal titles, page metadata (`title` / `description`), and static copy in exported spreadsheets used as documentation.
- **Code comments**: `//`, `/* */`, and JSDoc must be **English**; explain intent where non-obvious.
- **Tone**: professional, concise, consistent capitalization (sentence case for sentences).
- **No emoji** in code, comments, or UI strings (use Ant Design icons or text instead).

When touching shared export scripts, keep sheet row labels and notes in **English** so tooling stays aligned with the app UI language.
